AmigaCLISP 0.1 rc1 - GNU CLISP 2.49.95+ (ANSI Common Lisp) for AmigaOS 3.x

Needs: a 68040 (or better) and AmigaOS 3.x.
This build uses soft float; FPU use when present comes in a later release.

Install
  Copy the AmigaCLISP drawer where you want it, open a Shell there and type
    Execute Install
  This assigns CLISP: to the drawer (now and in S:User-Startup) and saves
  CLISP:lispinit.mem, the memory image CLISP starts from (about 15 s).

Use
  CLISP:CLISP              the Lisp prompt; (exit) leaves it
  CLISP:CLISP file.lisp    run a Lisp file
  Execute CLISP:MakeImage  make the memory image again (after an update)

Source and build: https://github.com/DalsinAI/amigaclisp
CLISP is free software under the GNU GPL (version 2 or later), as is this port.

